## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around operational risk in alert routing, including change control, cross-tenant impact, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model (evidence, lineage, owners)
- Lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and change control
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, MTTR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-like minimal CAPA create endpoint (illustrative)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const capa = req.body;
  // persist CAPA with evidence, lineage, owners
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', ...capa });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollback plan for alert-rule changes?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate containment and prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  redactionVersion: string;
  implicatedRegions: string[];
  tenantIds: string[];
  severity: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the effectiveness of the redaction rollback in production?
- Which metrics would you surface to product and compliance teams during a breach incident?

## Why This Is Asked
The question probes end-to-end CAPA thinking under regional backpressure failures, combining data modeling, lifecycle governance, and change management in a realistic latency-sensitive service.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle with gates and SLAs
- Canary rollout, rollback, and RCA templates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, lineage, owners, region } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA, link logs and policy references
  res.status(201).json({ id: 'capa-1234' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What metrics validate containment across regions?
- How would you automate evidence collection for CAPAs?
